hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15541","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Kathir al-Dari narrated to me, from Mujahid, he said: A shaykh who lived in Jahiliyyah, while we were in the expedition of Rhodes, called Ibn Abs narrated to us, he said: I was driving a cow for a family of ours, he said: Then I heard from its belly: Al Dharih, eloquent speech, a man shouting that there is no god but Allah. He said: So we came to Makkah and found that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had come forth."
